Yes — include `/hooks`, but keep it **small and client-only**.

For this app, hooks should be **UI behavior hooks only**, not data fetching, authz, payment, Stripe, Clerk, or Vouch lifecycle logic. Next’s App Router defaults pages/layouts to Server Components, and custom hooks/browser APIs belong in Client Components behind `"use client"`. citeturn810205search0turn810205search4

## Recommended `/hooks` cut

```txt
hooks/
  use-mobile.ts
  use-copy-to-clipboard.ts
  use-countdown.ts
  use-mounted.ts
  use-media-query.ts
```

## Why include these

| Hook | Keep? | Why |
|---|---:|---|
| `use-mobile.ts` | Yes | Useful for app shell/sidebar, mobile nav, drawer/sheet behavior. shadcn-style sidebars commonly expect a mobile breakpoint helper. |
| `use-media-query.ts` | Yes | More generic foundation than `use-mobile`; useful for future layout behavior. |
| `use-copy-to-clipboard.ts` | Yes | Core Vouch UX needs copy invite link / share link feedback. |
| `use-countdown.ts` | Yes | Confirmation window / deadline UI needs client-side ticking. |
| `use-mounted.ts` | Yes | Prevents hydration mismatch for client-only UI such as theme-dependent or viewport-dependent rendering. |

## Do **not** add these yet

```txt
use-current-user.ts
use-vouches.ts
use-payment-status.ts
use-authz.ts
use-confirm-presence.ts
use-stripe.ts
use-admin-data.ts
```

Those would fight the server-first architecture. Reads stay in `lib/fetcher/*`, writes stay in `lib/actions/*`, and authz stays server-side.

## Minimal hook files

### `hooks/use-media-query.ts`

```ts
"use client"

import { useEffect, useState } from "react"

export function useMediaQuery(query: string): boolean {
  const [matches, setMatches] = useState(false)

  useEffect(() => {
    const mediaQueryList = window.matchMedia(query)

    const handleChange = () => {
      setMatches(mediaQueryList.matches)
    }

    handleChange()
    mediaQueryList.addEventListener("change", handleChange)

    return () => {
      mediaQueryList.removeEventListener("change", handleChange)
    }
  }, [query])

  return matches
}
```

### `hooks/use-mobile.ts`

```ts
"use client"

import { useMediaQuery } from "@/hooks/use-media-query"

const MOBILE_BREAKPOINT = 768

export function useIsMobile(): boolean {
  return useMediaQuery(`(max-width: ${MOBILE_BREAKPOINT - 1}px)`)
}
